---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security"
  description="The mdbase Connect trust model for local collections, hosted collections, application grants, relay encryption, and notifications."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow"><i></i> Connect protocol 1</p>
        <h1>Trust the component that can open the data.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero__aside">
        <p>
          Connect keeps authorization enforcement at the local connector or
          hosted provider. It minimizes control-plane data, encrypts local relay
          payloads end to end, and names the hosted provider's trust boundary
          directly.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/sdk/security/">Developer guidance</a>
          <a class="button" href="https://github.com/mdbase-dev/mdbase-connect/tree/main/docs">
            Architecture documents
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Data boundaries</h2>
    <table class="trust-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Data</th>
          <th>Local collection</th>
          <th>Hosted collection</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Markdown records</td>
          <td>Remain on the registered computer</td>
          <td>Encrypted at rest in the hosted provider</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Absolute paths</td>
          <td>Remain at the local connector</td>
          <td>Not applicable to provider-backed records</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Operation payloads</td>
          <td>Encrypted app to connector across relay</td>
          <td>Sent directly to the grant-bound provider</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Grant policy</td>
          <td>Cached and rechecked locally</td>
          <td>Rechecked by the hosted provider</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Notification signals</td>
          <td colspan="2">Opaque signal, criterion, grant, and cursor metadata; no record path or content</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>What application developers must do</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Request the narrowest useful operation set.</h3>
          <p>
            Use contract-scoped access unless the feature truly needs
            collection-wide types or saved views. Ask for additional operations
            when the user opens the feature that needs them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Keep authorization state in an appropriate storage boundary.</h3>
          <p>
            Browser defaults use localStorage plus non-extractable IndexedDB
            keys. Native shells should provide storage and navigation adapters
            that match their platform security model.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Treat notifications as wake-up hints.</h3>
          <p>
            Never infer private state from a signal. Open the application, renew
            authorization if needed, and read the latest authorized collection
            state.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Use revision preconditions for writes.</h3>
          <p>
            Preserve the revision returned by reads and queries, then pass{" "}
            <code>if_revision</code> to update, rename, and delete operations.
            Resolve conflicts explicitly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
